= Daily Meals and Travel Per Diems

== The Individual Meal Allowance Framework

When traveling away from your regular office city on approved firm business, Noice & Toit LLP reimburses actual, necessary meal expenditures up to daily limits. Our philosophy focuses on providing wholesome, nourishing meals that support professional stamina while avoiding wasteful extravagance.

Reimbursement is based on actual itemized receipts rather than flat cash allowances, in compliance with international tax regimes. This chapter governs meals eaten alone. Meals with colleagues, clients, or candidates are governed by Figure 2 in Chapter 13, which also sets the alcohol allowances for each dining category.

== Daily Meal Allowance Caps

Daily meal thresholds are calibrated to reflect realistic business dining costs in metropolitan business centers. The limits cover food, non-alcoholic beverages, applicable sales taxes, and reimbursable gratuities:

=== Individual Meal Thresholds
- *Breakfast*: Up to *€15.00* / *\$18.00* / *£13.00*.
- *Lunch*: Up to *€25.00* / *\$30.00* / *£22.00*.
- *Dinner*: Up to *€45.00* / *\$55.00* / *£38.00*.
- *Maximum Daily Aggregate Cap*: *€85.00* / *\$100.00* / *£73.00* across all meals and snacks on one calendar day.

=== Which Cap Applies
The receipt time determines the meal category. A receipt timed before 11:00 is breakfast, from 11:00 to 15:59 is lunch, and from 16:00 onward is dinner. Where a restaurant bill lists a number of guests, the number of guests on the bill governs whether the meal is solo or group dining, unless the note states a different attendee count.

#card-do("Stay within daily meal spending caps")[
  Select quality, casual business dining that fits within our caps. After all deductions in this chapter, the remaining bill is reimbursed up to the cap for the meal category; the excess is deducted.
]

#card-dont("Roll over unspent meal allowances")[
  Unspent meal allowances cannot be accumulated, carried over into subsequent days, or converted into cash reimbursements. If you spend €10 on lunch, your dinner cap remains €45.00, not €60.00.
]

== Alcohol on Individual Solo Travel

Noice & Toit LLP maintains an unambiguous, firm-wide policy regarding alcoholic beverages consumed during individual travel.

#card-dont("Claim alcoholic beverages during solo dining")[
  Alcoholic beverages (beer, wine, cocktails, cider, spirits, and mixed drinks containing spirits) consumed while dining alone are strictly non-reimbursable. Finance deducts each alcoholic line at its gross price, plus any tax the receipt adds on top of it, before applying the meal cap. Non-alcoholic beer, mocktails, and 0% ABV drinks are ordinary beverages.
]

=== Auditing and Line-Item Reductions
Finance reads every itemized line and recognizes alcohol by name (e.g., "IPA", "Merlot", "Pilsner", "Highball", "Spritz", "Wein", "Sake"). If a summary card slip is submitted instead of an itemized bill, Finance cannot verify the absence of alcohol and rejects the line under Chapter 2.

== Gratuities, Service Charges, and Local Tipping Norms

Tipping practices vary substantially across global jurisdictions. Gratuities are reimbursable when they align with local customs. The tip cap is calculated on the bill total before tip (subtotal plus any taxes the receipt adds on top), and the tip amount above the cap is deducted. Where the tip is not printed on the receipt, no tip is reimbursed.

=== North American Norms (United States and Canada)
- In restaurants with table service, tips of up to 20% of the pre-tip bill are reimbursable.
- For counter service, takeout, and delivery, tips above \$1.00 are deducted.

=== European and United Kingdom Norms
- In European Union countries and Switzerland, menu prices legally include tax and service. Discretionary tips of up to 10% of the pre-tip bill are reimbursable; anything above 10% is deducted.
- Germany is a country-specific exception to this regional norm: the German cap is *20% of the pre-tip bill*, not 10%. The Global Tipping Standards table in Chapter 14 carries the German row, and its country-specific rows override these regional norms.
- In the United Kingdom, where an optional service charge (typically 12.5%) is printed on the bill, that service charge is reimbursable and any additional tip is deducted. Where no service charge is printed, a tip of up to 12.5% is reimbursable.
- Takeaway, counter service, and delivery orders anywhere in Europe carry no reimbursable tip.

=== Asian and Middle Eastern Norms
- In Japan, South Korea, Singapore, and Hong Kong, tipping is not customary. Any tip is deducted. A mandatory 10% service charge printed on the bill is reimbursable.

== Luxury Ingredients and the Truffle Rule

=== A Brief History
In the autumn of 2019, a three-person client dinner in Milan produced a bill on which a single risotto accounted for more than the combined airfare of the attendees. The dish was, by all accounts, excellent. The ensuing correspondence between the hosting partner, the Milan office administrator, the Head of Global Finance, and eventually the Audit Committee ran to forty-one e-mails, two of which contained photographs of the risotto. The Audit Committee concluded that the firm had no principled objection to truffles, only to the absence of a principle. Version 3.0 of this handbook introduced the Truffle Policy in response, and it has survived every subsequent revision unchanged in substance, if not in the volume of internal jokes it generates.

=== The Rule
The firm has no objection to good food, but certain ingredients turn a business meal into a tasting event. Dishes featuring truffle are evaluated under the Truffle Policy Flowchart, Figure 3 in Chapter 13, before any meal cap is applied. *The pass and fail thresholds for every truffle dish are not written in this chapter; they exist only inside the Figure 3 flowchart image, so inspect and read Figure 3 for each truffle line.* A dish that fails the flowchart is deducted at its gross line price like any other non-reimbursable item. The flowchart applies equally to solo meals, team dinners, and client hospitality.

- *Truffle dish on any meal*: inspect Figure 3 flowchart (Chapter 13).

== Working Late and Overtime Meals

When required to work in your regular office or home workspace past 20:30 on urgent client deliverables, you may claim one dinner or delivery order up to *€20.00 / \$25.00 / £18.00*, provided the note states that you were working late and names the matter. Alcohol is deducted as on any solo meal. Without such a statement, a restaurant receipt in your home office city is not a travel meal and is rejected.

== Dietary Requirements, Allergies, and Cultural Catering

The firm accommodates dietary requirements as a matter of professional courtesy and, where a medical or religious obligation applies, of basic workplace inclusion. Hosts ordering food for meetings, interviews, or working sessions plan for the group actually attending, not for a generic diner. People Operations maintains the Dietary Register for this purpose, and the Travel Desk will not release a catering order for an internal event until the host confirms the Register has been consulted.

