== Hydration and Long-Day Meal Scheduling

For all-day sessions, hosts are responsible for the shape of the catering day as much as its content. A session that runs from morning to evening with no planned rhythm produces the familiar pattern of a mid-morning sugar spike, a skipped midday break, and a room of decision-makers who agree to anything to reach the coffee. The Travel Desk publishes standard rhythms for common formats; hosts deviating from them state the reason in the event note.

Water must be available in the room for the entire duration of any session longer than two hours. The Sustainability Working Group supplies carafes and reusable cup sets on request; single-use bottled water requires a stated reason, such as an off-site without kitchen access. For evening sessions, the rhythm includes a substantial early-evening provision so that attendees are not kept at the table by the promise of food that never arrives.

