== Catering Workflow for Internal Events

Internal catering follows a short, deliberate sequence. The host consults the Dietary Register and the festival calendar, selects a vendor from the Approved Catering Directory, and submits the order through the Travel Desk portal at least five business days before the occasion, or two business days for short-notice service. The Travel Desk confirms the order, checks it against the Register extract for the attendee list, and returns objections within one business day. On the day, the host receives the delivery and afterwards files the event note recording what was served, for whom, and why.

The workflow distributes responsibility deliberately: no single person both orders the food and certifies that it met the attendees' declared needs.

