== Vendor Onboarding and Quality Review

New caterers are onboarded by the Travel Desk in a two-stage process. The first stage is documentary: the vendor provides food-safety certification, liability insurance, allergen management documentation, and references from two comparable corporate clients. The second stage is practical: the vendor caters two internal occasions under supervision, and the hosts file structured feedback on punctuality, labelling, temperature, and packaging. A vendor who clears both stages enters the directory as accredited; one who clears only the documentary stage stays probationary until the practical stage is complete.

Directory status is not permanent. The Travel Desk reviews every accredited vendor each quarter against its accumulated event notes, and the Sustainability Working Group contributes an assessment of packaging and food waste practices. Vendors with repeated punctuality or labelling failures move to under review, during which new event bookings are suspended; vendors who resolve the failures return to accredited, and vendors who do not are removed. Removal is recorded with reasons, because a vendor who fails quietly once tends to fail loudly later.

